  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-08-09T11:15:33.799Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Not sure it's 2019 problem, but i noticed when i make the trigger boxes ready for Quest side, i am surprised i am already bounced off and cannot go through trigger boxes.\nThen i discovered the problem applies only for looking down. If you look straight forward, you can walk through trigger box and it triggers correctly.\n\nBUT...\n\nIf you look down, the boxes turned in colliders, made you will bounced off and cannot get past it. \nThis will a problem if you make game or adventure world with a lot trigger boxes, the Quest users will experience nasty bounce offs (i mean you will pushed away) and so walking around a will big problem. This problem is not in PC side.\n\nIt's also weird to see the boxes act as colliders instead as trigger if you look down. Only straight forward has no problems. But it should not turn in collider if you look down. The boxes must stay as trigger and transparent.\n\nCan this problem fixed to avoid annoying moments in some game / adventure worlds? Actually every world who use trigger boxes to control some objects will have the problem.",
